{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403889-m20-forces","id":1403889,"title":"M20 Forces","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-21T14:58:43-07:00","id":1403889,"title":"M20 Forces","content":"Trying to get a full list of all the kinds of forces a mage can influence. The book lists a good amount and Ive added one or two I think makes sense. Starting up a new campaign and could use all the help I can get.<br /> <br /> Fire, Air, Momentum, Gravity, Radiation, Light, Sound, Magnetism, Radiation, Radiowaves, Pressure,<br /> <br /> Please help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T15:23:10-07:00","id":1403893,"title":"","content":"I know the answer is matter for this one, but I really love the idea of forces also being able to manipulate tension to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:44:45-07:00","id":1404160,"title":"","content":"Technically, depending on your paradigm something like darkness counts as a force","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T22:38:56-07:00","id":1404176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Actual_Table</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403889-m20-forces?p=1403893#post1403893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the answer is matter for this one, but I really love the idea of forces also being able to manipulate tension to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically? It does. Teeeechnically. Because teeeeeeechnically, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strong_interaction\" target=\"_blank\">strong nuclear force</a> as well as the Quantum Mechancial effect of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pauli_exclusion_principle#Stability_of_matter\" target=\"_blank\">Pauli Exclusion Principle</a> would fall under Forces in the real world. The first is what makes atoms tie together, the second is what prevents two pieces of matter from occupying the same space. It's what prevents atoms and molecues from actually ever literally touching - in the macroscopic world it's what prevents you from literally stepping through a wall. Or, you know, your structure from collapsing into a microscopic...strange state.<br /> <br /> But that would horribly complicate the Mage Forces Sphere, and also diminish the Matter sphere to just 'conjure and remove matter'<br /> So in a way, the sphere of Matter is a strange half-variant of the Forces sphere as it encompasses both actual matter particles and certain forces regarding them.<br /> Teeeechnically.<br /> <br /> There is one more obvious and more simple force that kind of falls on the edge between Matter and Forces, and that is: Friction, as with Spheres you can either see it as the property of an object (Matter) or as an interaction force between two objects (Forces). Usually it gets handled as a pure Matter sphere thing for simplicity's sake, just like mass and inertiaare simply seen as 'Matter' properties.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> But, let's keep things simple and by-the-book! The TL;DR answer to the OP question is '<b>if, in the real world, it isn't made of matter, or the isolated property of a piece of matter, it's goverend by Forces</b>'.<br /> <br /> <i>Gravity, radioactivty, visible (to the human eye) light, darkness, sound, silence, pressure, kinetic force, x-rays, radio, heat, cold, infrared, ultraviolet, magnetism, electricity (and the resulting electromagnetism of the former two), optionally frinction.</i><br /> The 'opposites' in that list (cold, darkness, silence..) are not part of the classic scientific literal 'forces' but as Stanlemon said, depending on mystics paradigm they *are* and can be treated as a thing created and manipulated by the Forces sphere.<br /> <br /> Note that 'Radioactivity' is listed under Forces here in the sense of 'Radioactive radiation', but to actually make material that is by its very nature classic &quot;bad radioactive&quot; requires Matter 5.<br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-23-2020, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T07:13:42-07:00","id":1404236,"title":"","content":"Huh. Yeah, that sounds right, and is a lot more simple than I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T09:48:40-07:00","id":1405079,"title":"","content":"Doesn't 'forces' include concepts that scientifically would be identical to another but for metaphysical purposes are different (aspects of cold and ice for example. Even flame and heat IIRC can be treated as separate things. IIRC light and shadow/dark are another such. Pressure may or may not be one of those things mentioned, although its technically shaping the intensity or focus of force/energy.. more specifically the former in a scientific sense. That tends to be covered by the level of skill in forces I think?) Presumably this can also involve chemical reactions as well as molecular and nuclear forces (or stuff beyond that as Ambrosia mentioned.) <br /> <br /> This could be.. interesting given how it can overlap with other spheres ('forces' dominante living beings.. electrical fields, chemical reactions, and the like) its definitely something you could rules lawyer if you tried hard enough, so I suspect a complete list isn't likely either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:17:00-07:00","id":1405159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403889-m20-forces?p=1405079#post1405079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't 'forces' include concepts that scientifically would be identical to another but for metaphysical purposes are different (aspects of cold and ice for example. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I'm thinking that cold is manipulated with Forces Magick, while for ice it is Matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:20:30-07:00","id":1405383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403889-m20-forces?p=1405159#post1405159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. I'm thinking that cold is manipulated with Forces Magick, while for ice it is Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word your looking for is temperature. So while a mage with forces could say shoot an icicle at you as an elemental attack they would need matter to make a permanent wall of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:24:04-07:00","id":1405384,"title":"","content":"\u201cTemperature\u201d is the scientific name for it, yes. But there are mystical worldviews where \u201ccold\u201d is a Force in its own right, in direct opposition to but distinct from \u201cheat\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}